# Formatting Standards

## Indentation

Use **2-space** indentation everywhere. Never tabs.

## Function Comments

Add a single-line comment above every function describing what it does.

```javascript
// Returns the rock mesh scaled for the given world chunk
function createRock(scale) {
  // ...
}
```

## Long Functions

Break long functions with hard returns so related sections are visually grouped. Prefer early returns and blank lines between logical steps over dense blocks.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — dense, hard to scan
function updateTrees(delta) {
  for (const tree of trees) { tree.rotation.y += delta; if (tree.ready) tree.update(delta); applyWind(tree); }
}

// ✅ GOOD — hard returns between steps
function updateTrees(delta) {
  for (const tree of trees) {
    tree.rotation.y += delta;

    if (!tree.ready) continue;

    tree.update(delta);
    applyWind(tree);
  }
}
```

## HTML Strings

Build HTML across multiple lines for readability. Do not pack an entire markup string onto one line.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
el.innerHTML = `<div class="panel"><h2>${title}</h2><p>${body}</p><button type="button">OK</button></div>`;

// ✅ GOOD
el.innerHTML = `
  <div class="panel">
    <h2>${title}</h2>
    <p>${body}</p>
    <button type="button">OK</button>
  </div>
`;
```
